 ### Pseudo-marginal Metropolis Light Transport (PSSMLT)
-Uses unbiased estimators of the scalar contribution function to allow for valid MCMC sampling even when the exact contribution is intractable. It extends PSSMLT by employing unbiased estimators, allowing for larger families of path space MLT and ERPT methods. [Pseudo-marginal Metropolis Light Transport (PSSMLT)](12276-pseudo-marginal-metropolis-light-transport-pssmlt.md)
+Uses unbiased estimators of the scalar contribution function to allow for valid MCMC sampling even when the exact contribution is intractable. It extends PSSMLT by employing unbiased estimators, allowing for larger families of path space MLT and ERPT methods. Choose it when the underlying path tracer requires unbiased transmission estimates to maintain correct MCMC targets. [Pseudo-marginal Metropolis Light Transport (PSSMLT)](12276-pseudo-marginal-metropolis-light-transport-pssmlt.md)
 
 ### Metropolis Light Transport
-The original MLT method that samples directly in path space. PSSMLT is an alternative that operates in primary sample space, which is easier to implement but may have limited exploration. [Metropolis Light Transport](12286-metropolis-light-transport.md)
+The original MLT method that samples directly in path space. PSSMLT is an alternative that operates in primary sample space, which is easier to implement but may have limited exploration. Choose it when direct path space mutation is feasible and maximum path space coverage is required. [Metropolis Light Transport](12286-metropolis-light-transport.md)
 
